hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17662","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, who said: I heard 'Abbad ibn Sharhabil, and he was from us, from Banu Gh ubar, who said: A year of famine struck us, so I came to Madinah, entered a garden among its gardens, took an ear of grain, rubbed it, ate from it, and carried some in my garment. The owner of the garden came, beat me, and took my garment. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You neither taught him when he was ignorant nor fed him when he was hungry or famished. He returned my garment to me and ordered for me half a wasq or a wasq."
